{"id":"2026-11-22-RS","date":"2026-11-22","ticker":"RS","name":"Reliance","sector":"Materials","industry":"Steel","price":398.46,"price_date":"2026-11-20","timeframe_days":182,"headline":"Reliance's sales growth sped up for five quarters to 43%, metal prices are rising faster than planned, and the stock has pulled back to its 200-day average","side":"long","timeframe":"About 6 months, through the next two quarterly reports","thesis":"Reliance's sales growth has sped up five quarters in a row, from flat to 7%, 12%, 16%, 27% and now 43% in the September quarter, when sales hit a record $5.2B. Two things are working at once. Prices rose 8.2% from the June quarter against a plan of flat to up 2%, and it shipped a record amount of metal, with tons up 15.6% from a year ago against 10.1% for the industry. Adjusted earnings per share rose 120% to $8.02, beating its own $6.40 to $6.60 guide, even after $2.74 a share of inventory accounting costs against $1.10 planned. The stock ran to 448 after the report and has since slipped to 398, back near its 200-day average, while trading at 18.2 times earnings, below its median of 19.1. The pullback gives a better entry into a business whose growth is still speeding up.","wrong_if":"A close under 362 would break the 60-day low of about 384 and the 200-day average with room to spare, and the trend would be over. The idea is also wrong if carbon steel prices fall from here in the December quarter or if tons sold drop below the industry, because both price and volume are holding up the case.","business":"Reliance is the largest metals service center company in North America. It buys steel, aluminum, stainless steel, copper, titanium and other metals in bulk from mills, then cuts and processes them to order and delivers small lots, mostly to machine shops and fabricators. Its end markets include construction, aerospace, energy, semiconductor plants, industrial machinery and transportation. Much of what it sells gets some processing first, which lets it charge more than a plain distributor.","segments_note":"Carbon steel, the biggest line at $3.1B, grew 54% in the September quarter, up from 28% in June and 14% a year ago. Aluminum grew 39% and stainless steel 30%, and both sped up. Even the small toll processing business, which processes metal customers already own, grew 14%. Data centers, energy projects and public construction drove demand.","growth_note":"Sales were $5.2B, up 43%, the fifth speed-up in a row. Gross margin was 31.6% on a basis that strips out inventory accounting (called FIFO), which is high for the business. The inventory charge (called LIFO, which books recent higher costs first) was $2.74 a share against $1.10 planned and the full-year estimate rose to $450M. That charge rises when prices rise, so it hides some of the real earnings gain. Border wall steel work added $0.74 a share in the quarter.","commentary":[{"point":"Record sales, record tons sold and adjusted earnings per share of $8.02, up 120% from a year ago.","speaker":"Karla Lewis, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Tons sold rose 4.3% from the June quarter to a record, and data centers, energy infrastructure and public construction kept demand strong despite tight supply.","speaker":"Stephen Koch, Reliance executive","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Sales grew 43%. The inventory charge was $2.74 a share against $1.10 in guidance, a $1.64 a share drag, and the full-year charge estimate is now $450M.","speaker":"Arthur Ajemyan, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"December quarter guidance is earnings per share of $7.40 to $7.60, including about $0.70 from the border wall project, which is about halfway through its first phase. The buyback limit rose to $2.5B.","speaker":"Reliance management","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Called it an exceptional quarter and credited its scale and long relationships with mills for getting metal to customers when supply is short.","speaker":"Karla Lewis, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said gross profit per ton stayed historically strong in aluminum and kept rising in carbon and stainless steel.","speaker":"Arthur Ajemyan, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"}],"tone_note":"The tone swung sharply upward: net tone went from 40 to 127 to 138 over the last three calls, and the answers to analysts were 77 points more upbeat than the call before. That is one of the biggest jumps in answer tone in this batch, and it lines up with a quarter that beat the company's own guide by more than $1 a share.","technical_note":"The stock closed at 398.46, below its 50-day average (410.34) but above its 200-day average (375.83), which is still rising. It ran to about 448 after the October 22 report and has since pulled back about 11%, so RSI has cooled to 36. The 60-day low is about 384. Over a year it beat the S&P 500 by 45 points and materials stocks by 32. The 52-week high is 454.93.","valuation_note":"At 18.2 times trailing earnings, Reliance is just under its median of 19.1. Trailing earnings still carry the large inventory charge, so the price is lower on an underlying basis. A steel price peak is the main reason the multiple would fall.","levels":{"entry_lo":385,"entry_hi":405,"stop":362,"target":460,"note":"Buy between 385 and 405, the area around the 60-day low and just above the 200-day average. The stop at 362 is about two daily ranges below the 60-day low and under the 200-day average. The target of 460 is just above the 52-week high of 454.93. From the posted price that is about $62 of upside for $36 of risk, or 1.7 to 1."},"risks":["Steel prices move in cycles. If carbon steel prices peak, sales growth would slow fast and the inventory charge would shrink only slowly.","The border wall work adds about $0.70 a share a quarter and will end when the project does.","December is a slow season, and the company already guided earnings below September.","Tariff changes on imported steel could lower the prices it can charge.","Not known from the brief: how much of the price gain comes from tariffs, the 2027 outlook, and when the border wall work ends."],"catalysts":["The December quarter report, likely in February 2027, against the $7.40 to $7.60 guide.","Monthly steel price data and mill price announcements.","Updates on data center and energy construction, the main demand drivers named on the call."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-19","adj_eps_name":"Non-GAAP diluted EPS","quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2023Q4","end":"2023-12-31","rev":3337.3,"gm":30.6,"om":9.7,"nm":8.2,"eps":4.7,"adj_eps":4.73,"rev_yoy":-7.6,"eps_yoy":-19.4},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q1","end":"2024-03-31","rev":3644.8,"gm":31.0,"om":10.8,"nm":8.3,"eps":5.23,"adj_eps":5.3,"rev_yoy":-8.1,"eps_yoy":-16.8},{"q":"Jun '24","id":"FY2024Q2","end":"2024-06-30","rev":3643.3,"gm":29.8,"om":9.7,"nm":7.4,"eps":4.67,"adj_eps":4.65,"rev_yoy":-6.1,"eps_yoy":-28.4},{"q":"Sep '24","id":"FY2024Q3","end":"2024-09-30","rev":3420.3,"gm":29.4,"om":8.0,"nm":5.8,"eps":3.61,"adj_eps":3.64,"rev_yoy":-5.6,"eps_yoy":-27.2},{"q":"Dec '24","id":"FY2024Q4","end":"2024-12-31","rev":3126.6,"gm":28.3,"om":4.5,"nm":3.4,"eps":1.93,"adj_eps":2.22,"rev_yoy":-6.3,"eps_yoy":-53.1},{"q":"Mar '25","id":"FY2025Q1","end":"2025-03-31","rev":3484.7,"gm":29.7,"om":7.9,"nm":5.7,"eps":3.74,"adj_eps":3.77,"rev_yoy":-4.4,"eps_yoy":-28.9},{"q":"Jun '25","id":"FY2025Q2","end":"2025-06-30","rev":3659.8,"gm":29.7,"om":8.5,"nm":6.4,"eps":4.42,"adj_eps":4.43,"rev_yoy":0.5,"eps_yoy":-4.7},{"q":"Sep '25","id":"FY2025Q3","end":"2025-09-30","rev":3651.2,"gm":28.3,"om":7.1,"nm":5.2,"eps":3.59,"adj_eps":3.64,"rev_yoy":6.8,"eps_yoy":0.0},{"q":"Dec '25","id":"FY2025Q4","end":"2025-12-31","rev":3498.6,"gm":27.3,"om":4.8,"nm":3.3,"eps":2.22,"adj_eps":2.4,"rev_yoy":11.9,"eps_yoy":8.1},{"q":"Mar '26","id":"FY2026Q1","end":"2026-03-31","rev":4026,"gm":29.1,"om":9.1,"nm":6.6,"eps":5.1,"adj_eps":5.16,"rev_yoy":15.5,"eps_yoy":36.9},{"q":"Jun '26"